---
/**
 * Ambient backdrop: three overlapping colour fields echoing the glow Intel puts
 * behind the silicon on its product heroes.
 *
 * Static by design. Drifting these was measured at 32fps against 60 with the
 * motion removed — a large `filter: blur()` is re-rasterised every frame it
 * moves, and it compounded badly with the dialog's backdrop-filter, which then
 * had to re-blur a backdrop that never stopped changing (16fps with a dialog
 * open). Held still, the same blur costs nothing: the layer is rasterised once.
 *
 * Purely decorative, so it is hidden from assistive tech and never takes
 * pointer events.
 */
---

<div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="aurora__field aurora__field--1"></span>
  <span class="aurora__field aurora__field--2"></span>
  <span class="aurora__field aurora__field--3"></span>
</div>

<style>
  .aurora {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .aurora__field {
    position: absolute;
    display: block;
    width: 62vmax;
    height: 62vmax;
    border-radius: 50%;
    opacity: var(--aurora-opacity);
    filter: blur(var(--aurora-blur));
    /* Not a hint about future animation — nothing here animates. It promotes
       each field to its own layer so the blur is rasterised once and cached
       instead of being recomputed on every frame the page produces. Dropping
       it measured 31fps against 60. */
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .aurora__field--1 {
    top: -22vmax;
    left: -8vmax;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--aurora-1), transparent 68%);
  }

  .aurora__field--2 {
    top: -28vmax;
    right: -10vmax;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--aurora-2), transparent 68%);
  }

  /* Smaller and dimmer: a cool highlight below the header rather than a third
     full-strength wash. The 5.5rem is twice the page title's 2.75rem, in rem
     rather than vmax so the offset tracks the type instead of the viewport. */
  .aurora__field--3 {
    top: calc(2vmax + 5.5rem);
    left: 34%;
    width: 38vmax;
    height: 38vmax;
    opacity: calc(var(--aurora-opacity) * 0.6);
    background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--aurora-3), transparent 70%);
  }
</style>
